INSERT INTO SEED_NOTES (NOTE_ID, CLAIM_ID, DENIAL_ID, NOTE_TYPE, NOTE_TEXT, EVIDENCE_SUMMARY, CREATED_BY) VALUES ('NOTE-0103-001', 'CLM-2026-0103', 'DNL-003', 'AGENT_INVESTIGATION', 'INVESTIGATION SUMMARY — CLM-2026-0103 / DNL-003

DENIAL: CO-55 — Services not medically necessary. Payer remark: Post-surgical follow-up MRI and injection therapy not supported by documentation of clinical necessity beyond standard recovery period.

CLAIM DETAILS: Provider Dr. Kevin Marsh (NPI 5551234567), Peak Spine & Neurosurgery. Member David Thompson (MBR-1005), DOB 1970-02-14. DOS 2026-04-10. Total billed $8,200. Three lines: (1) 99215 Office visit high complexity $4,200, (2) 72148 MRI lumbar spine w/o contrast $2,800, (3) 20610 Arthrocentesis/injection major joint $1,200. All coded M54.5 (Low back pain).

ELIGIBILITY: Member active on ESSENTIAL-100 EPO plan (PAY-400), in-network. Deductible fully met ($1,000/$1,000). OOP at $2,500 of $8,000 max. Spine Surgery benefit requires auth; Post-Surgical Follow-up benefit does not require auth per eligibility table.

PRIOR AUTH: No prior authorization found for member MBR-1005. No auth on file matching this DOS or these CPT codes. Contract (CTR-003) requires prior auth for advanced diagnostic imaging and outpatient procedures over $3,000. MRI 72148 qualifies as advanced diagnostic imaging.

PAYER POLICY: Section 6.5 (Post-Operative Care Coverage) states post-op MRI and interventional procedures require documentation of medical necessity beyond standard recovery, specifically: (1) failure of expected recovery milestones, (2) new/worsening symptoms not attributable to normal post-op course, (3) clinical findings warranting further investigation. Section 6.2 requires documentation including chief complaint, history, exam findings, diagnostic results, assessment, and treatment plan rationale. Section 6.1 confirms medical necessity determinations follow evidence-based guidelines with peer-to-peer review available.

CLASSIFICATION: POTENTIAL_CLINICAL — CO-55 medical necessity denial requires clinical review. This agent is NOT making a clinical determination.

RECOMMENDATION: ROUTE_TO_CLINICAL — Clinical team should: (1) Gather supporting documentation (operative notes, progress notes showing post-surgical complications or stalled recovery, imaging reports), (2) Consider peer-to-peer review per payer Section 6.1, (3) If clinical support confirmed, file formal appeal per Section 8.2 within 90-day window (deadline approx. 2026-07-21). Appeal must include provider attestation, medical records, clinical guidelines, and any peer-to-peer notes.

URGENCY: HIGH — $8,200 at stake, appeal window is time-sensitive.', 'Member active/in-network on ESSENTIAL-100. No prior auth on file for MBR-1005. CO-55 medical necessity denial for post-surgical follow-up services (MRI lumbar spine + injection). Payer policy Sections 6.5, 6.2, 6.1 outline documentation requirements and appeal pathway. Contract CTR-003 confirms 90-day appeal window and 120-day filing limit. Denial history shows 1 similar CO-55 denial for PAY-400/PRV-520 with 0% overturn rate (limited data). Peer-to-peer review available per payer policy.', 'DENIAL_AGENT');
INSERT INTO SEED_NOTES (NOTE_ID, CLAIM_ID, DENIAL_ID, NOTE_TYPE, NOTE_TEXT, EVIDENCE_SUMMARY, CREATED_BY) VALUES ('NOTE-0203-001', 'CLM-2026-0203', 'DNL-010', 'AGENT_INVESTIGATION', 'INVESTIGATION SUMMARY — CLM-2026-0203 / DNL-010

Denial Code: CO-197 (Prior authorization was not obtained)
Denial Amount: $16,200.00
Date of Service: 2026-03-01
Procedures: CPT 23412 (Repair of rotator cuff, chronic) and CPT 29827 (Arthroscopy shoulder, rotator cuff repair)
Diagnosis: M75.11 (Rotator cuff tear, right shoulder)
Provider: Dr. Alan Prescott (NPI 1234567890), Metro Orthopedic Center, Group NPI GRP-4420
Payer: PAY-200 / PREMIER-500

ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS:
The claim was denied because no prior authorization was found linked to the rendering provider individual NPI. However, approved authorization AUTH-7744 EXISTS for this exact member (MBR-1007), these exact CPT codes (23412, 29827), this exact diagnosis (M75.11), and the date of service falls within the valid authorization period (2026-02-15 to 2026-04-15). The authorization was obtained under the GROUP NPI (GRP-4420), not the individual provider NPI (1234567890). The PRIOR_AUTH_ID field on the claim was submitted as NULL — the auth reference was never attached.

POLICY SUPPORT:
- Payer Policy Section 3.4 (Group vs Individual NPI Authorization Policy) explicitly states: authorizations obtained under a group NPI shall be accepted for claims submitted by any affiliated individual provider within the group.
- Section 3.6 (Finding Existing Authorizations) directs searching by group NPI when individual NPI yields no results.
- Section 4.1 (Corrected Claims and Resubmission) permits resubmission with correct auth reference within 90 days of denial date.
- Section 10.1 (Common Denial Codes) confirms CO-197 resolution path: search for auth under all associated NPIs.
- Contract CTR-001 NPI_POLICY confirms group-to-individual NPI cross-referencing is accepted.

CLASSIFICATION: TECHNICAL — NPI cross-reference / auth attachment error.
STRATEGY: CORRECT_AND_RESUBMIT — Resubmit claim with AUTH-7744 referenced, citing policy Sections 3.4, 3.6, and 4.1.
FILING WINDOW: 90 days from denial (2026-03-12), deadline approximately 2026-06-10. ~45 days remaining.
CONFIDENCE: 0.95', 'Auth AUTH-7744 found under group NPI GRP-4420 covering CPT 23412+29827 for MBR-1007, valid 2/15-4/15/2026. DOS 3/1 within range. Claim submitted without auth reference. Payer Sections 3.4, 3.6, 4.1, 10.1 and Contract CTR-001 NPI policy all support group-to-individual NPI cross-referencing. Recommend CORRECT_AND_RESUBMIT with auth reference. 3 similar CO-197 denials for this provider/payer with 0% overturn to date (none were appealed or resubmitted).', 'DENIAL_AGENT');
