-- SEED_APPEAL_DRAFTS (4 rows)
INSERT INTO SEED_APPEAL_DRAFTS (APPEAL_ID, CLAIM_ID, DENIAL_ID, APPEAL_TYPE, APPEAL_BODY, POLICY_CITATIONS, STATUS, CREATED_BY, DOCX_STAGE_PATH, REVIEW_STATUS, REVIEWER_NOTES, REVIEWED_AT) VALUES ('APL-0103-001', 'CLM-2026-0103', 'DNL-003', 'FORMAL_APPEAL', 'Essential Care Network
Appeals Department

RE: Appeal of Claim Denial — Medical Necessity
Claim ID: CLM-2026-0103
Denial ID: DNL-003
Member: David Thompson (MBR-1005), DOB: 02/14/1970
Plan: Essential Care 100 (ESSENTIAL-100)
Provider: Dr. Kevin Marsh, NPI 5551234567, Peak Spine & Neurosurgery
Date of Service: 04/10/2026
Total Billed: $8,200.00
Denial Code: CO-55 — Services not medically necessary

Dear Appeals Review Committee,

We are writing to formally appeal the denial of the above-referenced claim under denial code CO-55. The claim was denied with the remark that post-surgical follow-up MRI and injection therapy were not supported by documentation of clinical necessity beyond the standard recovery period.

SERVICES PROVIDED:
1. CPT 99215 — Office visit, established patient, high complexity ($4,200.00)
2. CPT 72148 — MRI lumbar spine without contrast ($2,800.00)
3. CPT 20610 — Arthrocentesis, aspiration and/or injection, major joint ($1,200.00)
All services were rendered for diagnosis M54.5 (Low back pain).

COVERAGE AND ELIGIBILITY:
Mr. Thompson is an active member on the Essential Care 100 EPO plan (PAY-400), effective 01/01/2026 with no term date. He is in-network with Peak Spine & Neurosurgery. His annual deductible of $1,000 has been fully met, and he has accumulated $2,500 toward his $8,000 out-of-pocket maximum. His plan includes both Spine Surgery and Post-Surgical Follow-up benefit categories.

BASIS FOR APPEAL:
Per your policy Section 6.5 (Post-Operative Care Coverage), additional diagnostic imaging and interventional procedures during the post-operative period require documentation demonstrating: (1) failure of expected recovery milestones, (2) new or worsening symptoms not attributable to normal post-operative course, and (3) clinical findings on examination that warrant further investigation.

Per Section 6.2 (Documentation Requirements for Medical Necessity), supporting documentation must include chief complaint, relevant history, physical examination findings, diagnostic test results, clinical assessment, and treatment plan rationale.

We respectfully submit that the enclosed clinical documentation [TO BE ATTACHED BY CLINICAL TEAM] demonstrates that Mr. Thompson''s post-surgical course warranted the additional diagnostic and therapeutic interventions performed on 04/10/2026.

[CLINICAL TEAM: Please insert here the specific clinical justification including: operative notes from the original surgery, post-operative progress notes documenting recovery concerns, physical examination findings from the 04/10/2026 visit, and any clinical guidelines supporting the medical necessity of these services. This section requires clinical review and attestation — the operations team has assembled the administrative evidence but is NOT making a clinical determination.]

Per Section 6.1 (Medical Necessity Determination Framework), we note that peer-to-peer review with a board-certified physician is available for disputed necessity decisions. We request a peer-to-peer review if this written appeal does not result in overturn of the denial.

Per Section 8.2 (Appeal Filing Requirements), this appeal is filed within the 90-day appeal window from the denial date of 04/22/2026. We have included the provider attestation letter, relevant medical records, and applicable clinical guidelines as required.

We respectfully request that Essential Care Network reverse the denial and process the claim for payment in accordance with Mr. Thompson''s plan benefits and the contracted allowed amounts.

Sincerely,

[Provider Signature Required]
Dr. Kevin Marsh
Peak Spine & Neurosurgery
NPI: 5551234567
Group NPI: GRP-6600

Enclosures: [TO BE COMPLETED BY CLINICAL TEAM]
- Provider attestation letter
- Operative notes from original surgery
- Post-operative progress notes
- Physical examination findings from 04/10/2026
- Relevant clinical guidelines/literature
- Peer-to-peer review notes (if applicable)', '6.5, 6.2, 6.1, 8.2, 6.7', 'DRAFT', 'DENIAL_AGENT', 'CLM-2026-0103/Appeal_CLM-2026-0103.docx', 'DRAFT', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO SEED_APPEAL_DRAFTS (APPEAL_ID, CLAIM_ID, DENIAL_ID, APPEAL_TYPE, APPEAL_BODY, POLICY_CITATIONS, STATUS, CREATED_BY, DOCX_STAGE_PATH, REVIEW_STATUS, REVIEWER_NOTES, REVIEWED_AT) VALUES ('APL-0301-001', 'CLM-2026-0301', 'DNL-011', 'FORMAL_APPEAL', 'Dear Claims Review Department,

Re: Formal Appeal — Claim CLM-2026-0301
Member: Jennifer Anderson (MBR-1006)
Plan: Value Care 250 (VALUE-250)
Provider: Dr. Rachel Owens, NPI 9876543210, Summit Cardiology Associates
Date of Service: March 15, 2026
Denial ID: DNL-011
Denial Code: CO-50 (Non-covered service)
Denied Amount: $19,500.00

We are writing to formally appeal the denial of claim CLM-2026-0301 for remote cardiac rhythm monitoring services (CPT 93229 and CPT 93228) rendered on March 15, 2026. The denial reason states that remote cardiac monitoring is not in the benefit schedule. We respectfully contend that this denial is incorrect and request immediate reconsideration.

GROUNDS FOR APPEAL:

1. SERVICE IS COVERED UNDER THE CARDIAC CARE RIDER (Section 7.3.2)
Your plan policy, Section 7.3.2 — Remote Cardiac Monitoring Services, explicitly states: "Remote cardiac rhythm monitoring (CPT 93224-93229) is a covered benefit under the Cardiac Care Rider when the following criteria are met." All four criteria are satisfied:

   (a) Ordered by a participating cardiologist: Dr. Rachel Owens is a participating cardiologist within your network at Summit Cardiology Associates.
